# v4 backend reference (OGen / Legacy)

**v4 / OGen / Legacy** is current production. **v5 / NextGen** is this monorepo. Vocabulary:
[abcmemory-vocabulary](/.cursor/rules/abcmemory-vocabulary.mdc). Layout:
[01](/docs/proposals/v4-to-v5-migration/01-legacy-repos-and-reference-setup.md).

## When to read

Open these trees for v4-to-v5 migration inventory, v4 billing carryover, or when the operator
asks for the v4 / OGen / Legacy backend. Do not browse them for ordinary NextGen tasks. Do not
edit or publish those checkouts.

| Path | Read for |
| ---- | -------- |
| `~/repos/pv/v4/podverse-api` | Entities, schema, scripts. Source of truth for columns. |
| `~/repos/pv/v4/podverse-web` | Consumer web |
| `~/repos/pv/v4/podverse-shared` | Shared types |
| `~/repos/pv/v4/podverse-ops` | Prod compose and env layout (no secret values) |
| `~/repos/pv/podverse-rn` | v4 mobile. Also **legacy-app-reference**. |

Confirm the checkout is on `develop` or `master`, not `v5-develop`. `v5-develop` is split-era
v5, not production v4. Prefer `podverse-api` entity files over guessed table names. v4 users
live in `users` (`email`, `membershipExpiration`). They do not live in `account_credentials`.

## `V4_DATABASE_URL`

The prod-copy database is a snapshot, not live production. It is named only by
**`V4_DATABASE_URL`**. Never commit the URL, a password, a dump, or a connection string.

The value lives in one home file, outside the repo:

`~/.config/podverse/v4-database-url`

That file is `KEY=value` plus `#` comments. Tokens still starting with `REPLACE_WITH_` mean
the file is unset. If the process environment is empty, read this file only. Do not search
the machine for another URL.

- Queries are read-only (`SELECT`, counts, null rates). No `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, or DDL.
- A connection error of "Operation not permitted" means this shell has no network
  (Ask mode, or a read-only sandbox whose allowlist does not include the Tailscale
  host). The URL file is still valid. Tailscale on the Mac does not reach through
  that sandbox. Retry in Agent mode. Do not look for another database URL, and do
  not treat an earlier successful read as proof that this shell can connect.
- If the variable is unset, leave the SQL in the doc and write "not run" in
  `docs/proposals/v4-to-v5-migration/_WAKE-UP.md`.
- Reports are counts, timings, and id-shaped keys only. No emails, names, tokens, or raw rows.
- Count output goes in `_WAKE-UP.md` (counts only) or under `.artifacts/v4-rehearsal-counts/`
  (already gitignored). Never commit a CSV of people.

## Out of scope here

Do not add migration workers, billing importers, or production writes from this reference.
Those wait for a later plan.
